  {
   "id": "Qnm8WBxqAgAJ",
   "from": "Thomas Feutrier",
   "author": "1d9f190c517292b6",
   "date": "2023-09-29T12:26:33Z",
   "subject": "PDF manual wrong issues",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hello,<br>I think I&#39;ve come across a bug in the pdf of the package manual on pages 32-33.<br>In order to retrieve the instance names, you do: <br><a href=\"http://pair.id\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://pair.id&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792481963631000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0Q0g8Y2uIQo5zP3ArNLGE3\">pair.id</a> &lt;- which(!<a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792481963631000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3Ygq2Sgj4cS50CFb30_uvK\">is.na</a>(all.exp))<br>AND you say that what we want to retrieve are the rownames that correspond to the Seed instances in instancesList.<br>However which() doesn&#39;t return the rowname but the index if the &quot;all.exp&quot; was a column by column vector, at least on my version of R.<br>The problem is that too many instances are retrieved in the case of a very large train set, and especially the wrong ones.<br>To fix this, all you have to do is:<br><a href=\"http://pair.id\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://pair.id&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792481963631000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0Q0g8Y2uIQo5zP3ArNLGE3\">pair.id</a> &lt;- which(!<a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792481963631000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3Ygq2Sgj4cS50CFb30_uvK\">is.na</a>(all.exp), arr.ind=TRUE)[, &quot;row&quot;]<br>And you&#39;ve got the rownames and the right number.<div><div>I can send the logfile and the executable code to test. Hoping that which works the same way on your computers.</div><div><br>Kind Regards,<br><div>Feutrier Thomas  <br></div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "rAIXE2ZzAgAJ",
   "from": "Manuel López-Ibáñez",
   "author": "854a0709976c2a48",
   "date": "2023-09-29T15:16:46Z",
   "subject": "Re: PDF manual wrong issues",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div>Hi Thomas,</div><div><br></div><div>Please do so. I cannot see where the text says that &#39;which&#39; returns rownames.</div><div><br></div><div>Could you open an issue? <a href=\"https://github.com/MLopez-Ibanez/irace/issues\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/MLopez-Ibanez/irace/issues&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792481963632000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1EEfWlGrIIcyZGUcJTJnmP\">https://github.com/MLopez-Ibanez/irace/issues</a></div><div><br></div><div>And point where in the user-guide source file you think the error may be?</div><div><br></div><div>This is where the line that you mention is located:</div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"https://github.com/MLopez-Ibanez/irace/blob/35d09d9d0b175b055a5421aac4f46c15cbd152db/vignettes/irace-package.Rnw#L2024\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/MLopez-Ibanez/irace/blob/35d09d9d0b175b055a5421aac4f46c15cbd152db/vignettes/irace-package.Rnw%23L2024&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792481963633000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2IvsYjFD1ikPFzuUoH59pg\">https://github.com/MLopez-Ibanez/irace/blob/35d09d9d0b175b055a5421aac4f46c15cbd152db/vignettes/irace-package.Rnw#L2024</a></div><div><br></div><div></div><div>Thanks!</div><div><br></div><div>Manuel.<br></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Friday, 29 September 2023 at 13:26:33 UTC+1 Thomas Feutrier wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">Hello,<br>I think I&#39;ve come across a bug in the pdf of the package manual on pages 32-33.<br>In order to retrieve the instance names, you do: <br><a href=\"http://pair.id\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://pair.id&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792481963633000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0i1y8k3HQwtobDwepyl1lB\">pair.id</a> &lt;- which(!<a href=\"http://is.na\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792481963633000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3q3nod2fRbLwFZbpwabcok\">is.na</a>(all.exp))<br>AND you say that what we want to retrieve are the rownames that correspond to the Seed instances in instancesList.<br>However which() doesn&#39;t return the rowname but the index if the &quot;all.exp&quot; was a column by column vector, at least on my version of R.<br>The problem is that too many instances are retrieved in the case of a very large train set, and especially the wrong ones.<br>To fix this, all you have to do is:<br><a href=\"http://pair.id\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://pair.id&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792481963633000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0i1y8k3HQwtobDwepyl1lB\">pair.id</a> &lt;- which(!<a href=\"http://is.na\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792481963633000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3q3nod2fRbLwFZbpwabcok\">is.na</a>(all.exp), arr.ind=TRUE)[, &quot;row&quot;]<br>And you&#39;ve got the rownames and the right number.<div><div>I can send the logfile and the executable code to test. Hoping that which works the same way on your computers.</div><div><br>Kind Regards,<br><div>Feutrier Thomas  <br></div><br></div></div></blockquote></div>"
    ]
   ]
