  {
   "id": "eGbgdxAEAwAJ",
   "from": "Manuel López-Ibáñez",
   "author": "854a0709976c2a48",
   "date": "2023-10-01T11:27:47Z",
   "subject": "Re: PDF manual wrong issues",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<p dir=\"auto\">Hi Thomas,</p>\r\n<p dir=\"auto\">The example there is designed to work when <span>all.exp</span> is a vector, so <span><a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792481963642000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3nyATXBFSu3MyGHi7LJhjt\">is.na</a>()</span> and <span>which()</span> return vectors.</p>\r\n<p dir=\"auto\">If you select two configurations or more, then <span>all.exp</span> is a matrix and, you would need to choose of these two options:</p>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><span><span><span>#</span> You want instances where all configurations have been evaluated:</span>\r\n<span><br></span></span></div><div dir=\"auto\"><span><span><a href=\"http://pair.id\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://pair.id&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792481963642000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2k9EMaWNQlFtZ7njpnQIdg\">pair.id</a></span> <span>&lt;-</span> which(apply(<span>!</span><a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792481963642000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3nyATXBFSu3MyGHi7LJhjt\">is.na</a>(<span>all.exp</span>), <span>1</span>, <span>all</span>)) <br></span></div><div dir=\"auto\"><span><span><span>#</span> You want instances where at least one configuration has been evaluated:</span> <br></span></div><div dir=\"auto\"><span><span><a href=\"http://pair.id\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://pair.id&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792481963642000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2k9EMaWNQlFtZ7njpnQIdg\">pair.id</a></span> <span>&lt;-</span> which(apply(<span>!</span><a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792481963642000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3nyATXBFSu3MyGHi7LJhjt\">is.na</a>(<span>all.exp</span>), <span>1</span>, <span>any</span>))</span><div>\r\n    </div></div><div>For the next version of irace, I am going to change this example to make the above clearer.</div><div><br></div><div>I hope the above helps!</div><div><br></div><div>Manuel<br></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Friday, 29 September 2023 at 23:10:13 UTC+1 Thomas Feutrier wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div><div><div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-variant-alternates:normal;vertical-align:baseline\">Hello again,</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-variant-alternates:normal;vertical-align:baseline\">You can try this logFile: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ihbeKFxCdK9A-ZHGWpZ06zUYmi_Lbjgh/view?usp=sharing\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ihbeKFxCdK9A-ZHGWpZ06zUYmi_Lbjgh/view?usp%3Dsharing&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792481963642000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1u7ZApI64PBCW_7htcdKOz\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ihbeKFxCdK9A-ZHGWpZ06zUYmi_Lbjgh/view?usp=sharing</a></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-variant-alternates:normal;vertical-align:baseline\"><br></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-variant-alternates:normal;vertical-align:baseline\">and execute these lines:</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-variant-alternates:normal;vertical-align:baseline\">all.exp &lt;- iraceResults$experiments[,as.character(c(1,2,3))]</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-variant-alternates:normal;vertical-align:baseline\">all.exp</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-variant-alternates:normal;vertical-align:baseline\"><a href=\"http://pair.id\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://pair.id&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792481963642000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2k9EMaWNQlFtZ7njpnQIdg\">pair.id</a> &lt;- which(!<a href=\"http://is.na\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792481963642000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3nyATXBFSu3MyGHi7LJhjt\">is.na</a>(all.exp),arr.ind = TRUE)[,&quot;row&quot;]</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-variant-alternates:normal;vertical-align:baseline\"><a href=\"http://pair.id\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://pair.id&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792481963642000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2k9EMaWNQlFtZ7njpnQIdg\">pair.id</a> &lt;- which(!<a href=\"http://is.na\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792481963642000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3nyATXBFSu3MyGHi7LJhjt\">is.na</a>(all.exp))</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-variant-alternates:normal;vertical-align:baseline\"><a href=\"http://pair.id\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://pair.id&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792481963642000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2k9EMaWNQlFtZ7njpnQIdg\">pair.id</a></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-variant-alternates:normal;vertical-align:baseline\">#Get index of each instance used</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-variant-alternates:normal;vertical-align:baseline\">index_instances &lt;- iraceResults$state$.irace$instancesList[<a href=\"http://pair.id\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://pair.id&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792481963642000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2k9EMaWNQlFtZ7njpnQIdg\">pair.id</a>, &quot;instance&quot;]</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-variant-alternates:normal;vertical-align:baseline\">tmp &lt;- iraceResults$scenario$instances[index_instances]</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-variant-alternates:normal;vertical-align:baseline\">You will see that with the version in the pdf: you get 25 instances used while the matrix all.exp shows that there are 10 on the first three config.</span></p><br></div></div></div><div>Feutrier Thomas</div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\">Le vendredi 29 septembre 2023 à 17:16:46 UTC+2, Manuel López-Ibáñez a écrit :<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div>Hi Thomas,</div><div><br></div><div>Please do so. I cannot see where the text says that &#39;which&#39; returns rownames.</div><div><br></div><div>Could you open an issue? <a href=\"https://github.com/MLopez-Ibanez/irace/issues\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/MLopez-Ibanez/irace/issues&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792481963642000&amp;usg=AOvVaw28T8NvDDD26qcjIyhb27pi\">https://github.com/MLopez-Ibanez/irace/issues</a></div><div><br></div><div>And point where in the user-guide source file you think the error may be?</div><div><br></div><div>This is where the line that you mention is located:</div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"https://github.com/MLopez-Ibanez/irace/blob/35d09d9d0b175b055a5421aac4f46c15cbd152db/vignettes/irace-package.Rnw#L2024\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/MLopez-Ibanez/irace/blob/35d09d9d0b175b055a5421aac4f46c15cbd152db/vignettes/irace-package.Rnw%23L2024&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792481963642000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2u3aUWRZm5I86CScuuc_l6\">https://github.com/MLopez-Ibanez/irace/blob/35d09d9d0b175b055a5421aac4f46c15cbd152db/vignettes/irace-package.Rnw#L2024</a></div><div><br></div><div></div><div>Thanks!</div><div><br></div><div>Manuel.<br></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Friday, 29 September 2023 at 13:26:33 UTC+1 Thomas Feutrier wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">Hello,<br>I think I&#39;ve come across a bug in the pdf of the package manual on pages 32-33.<br>In order to retrieve the instance names, you do: <br><a href=\"http://pair.id\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://pair.id&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792481963642000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2k9EMaWNQlFtZ7njpnQIdg\">pair.id</a> &lt;- which(!<a href=\"http://is.na\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792481963642000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3nyATXBFSu3MyGHi7LJhjt\">is.na</a>(all.exp))<br>AND you say that what we want to retrieve are the rownames that correspond to the Seed instances in instancesList.<br>However which() doesn&#39;t return the rowname but the index if the &quot;all.exp&quot; was a column by column vector, at least on my version of R.<br>The problem is that too many instances are retrieved in the case of a very large train set, and especially the wrong ones.<br>To fix this, all you have to do is:<br><a href=\"http://pair.id\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://pair.id&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792481963642000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2k9EMaWNQlFtZ7njpnQIdg\">pair.id</a> &lt;- which(!<a href=\"http://is.na\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792481963642000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3nyATXBFSu3MyGHi7LJhjt\">is.na</a>(all.exp), arr.ind=TRUE)[, &quot;row&quot;]<br>And you&#39;ve got the rownames and the right number.<div><div>I can send the logfile and the executable code to test. Hoping that which works the same way on your computers.</div><div><br>Kind Regards,<br><div>Feutrier Thomas  <br></div><br></div></div></blockquote></div></blockquote></div></blockquote></div>"
